{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.HeckeH3","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HeckeH3","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.HeckeRep","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.Trace","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":26,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.axialCouplingAlgebraic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.axialCouplingAlgebraic","kind":"def","line":332,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HeckeH3.lean#L332-L348","doc":"The axial coupling ratio (over the fraction field):\n\n`g_A / g_V = (5/3) × |tr_std(β_color)| / |tr_sym(β_color)|`\n\nIn the fraction field of `ℤ[t, t⁻¹]`, the ratio\n`tr_std / (3)` is computed exactly.\n\nThe 5/3 prefactor (naive quark model) and absolute value\nare applied in the numerical evaluation (Chapter 7).\n\nHere we compute the algebraic ratio:\n`r(q) = tr_std(h₀₁ + h₁₂ + h₀₂) / 3`\n\nwhich is an element of the fraction field. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.borromeanColorSum_trivTrace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.borromeanColorSum_trivTrace","kind":"def","line":326,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HeckeH3.lean#L326-L330","doc":"The trivial representation trace of the Borromean color sum.\n\nEach half-Borromean evaluates to 1 in the trivial rep,\nso the sum is 3. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.borromeanColorSum_stdTrace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.borromeanColorSum_stdTrace","kind":"def","line":320,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HeckeH3.lean#L320-L324","doc":"The standard representation trace of the Borromean color sum.\n\n`tr_std(h₀₁ + h₁₂ + h₀₂)` as an element of `ℤ[t, t⁻¹]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.halfBorromeanConj_trivial_eval","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.halfBorromeanConj_trivial_eval","kind":"theorem","line":301,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HeckeH3.lean#L301-L316","doc":"Every conjugated half-Borromean also evaluates to the identity\nin the trivial representation (same reasoning: commutator in\nabelian rep). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.halfBorromean_trivial_eval","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.halfBorromean_trivial_eval","kind":"theorem","line":277,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HeckeH3.lean#L277-L299","doc":"Every half-Borromean evaluates to the identity in the trivial representation.\n\nIn the trivial rep, σ_i ↦ q · I, σ_i⁻¹ ↦ q⁻¹ · I.\nSo h_{ij} = σ_i⁻¹ σ_j σ_i σ_j⁻¹ ↦ q⁻¹ · q · q · q⁻¹ · I = I.\n\nThis holds because every half-Borromean is a commutator, and\nany commutator is trivial in a 1-dimensional (abelian)\nrepresentation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.borromeanColorSum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.borromeanColorSum","kind":"def","line":265,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HeckeH3.lean#L265-L273","doc":"The Borromean color average in the standard representation:\n`β_color = ⅓(h₀₁ + h₁₂ + h₀₂)`.\n\nSince we work over ℤ[t, t⁻¹] (no division by 3), we store\nthe UN-AVERAGED sum.  The factor of 3 is handled in the ratio\ncomputation (it cancels between numerator and denominator when\nboth channels use the same average). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.halfBorromeanStd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.halfBorromeanStd","kind":"def","line":259,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HeckeH3.lean#L259-L263","doc":"The half-Borromean matrix for each color tube. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.instReprColorTube","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.instReprColorTube","kind":"instance","line":257,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HeckeH3.lean#L257-L257","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.instReprColorTube.repr","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.instReprColorTube.repr","kind":"def","line":257,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HeckeH3.lean#L257-L257","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.instDecidableEqColorTube","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.instDecidableEqColorTube","kind":"instance","line":257,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HeckeH3.lean#L257-L257","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.ColorTube.rb","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.ColorTube.rb","kind":"ctor","line":256,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HeckeH3.lean#L256-L256","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.ColorTube.gb","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.ColorTube.gb","kind":"ctor","line":255,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HeckeH3.lean#L255-L255","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.ColorTube.rg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.ColorTube.rg","kind":"ctor","line":254,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HeckeH3.lean#L254-L254","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.ColorTube","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.ColorTube","kind":"inductive","line":244,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HeckeH3.lean#L244-L257","doc":"The three color-tube half-Borromean matrices in the standard\nrepresentation.\n\nEach half-Borromean corresponds to one of the 3 color tubes\nof the exceptional divisor on Σ₄:\n\n- h₀₁ = σ₀⁻¹ σ₁ σ₀ σ₁⁻¹   (adjacent pair, standard)\n- h₁₂ = σ₁⁻¹ σ₀ σ₁ σ₀⁻¹   (adjacent pair, swapped)\n- h₀₂ = σ₀⁻¹ σ₁⁻¹ σ₀ σ₁   (non-adjacent pair, conjugated) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.stdRep3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.stdRep3","kind":"def","line":223,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HeckeH3.lean#L223-L240","doc":"The standard (2,1) representation of H₃(q) as a `HeckeRep` instance. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.stdRep3_chi_borromean_eq_trace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.stdRep3_chi_borromean_eq_trace","kind":"theorem","line":210,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HeckeH3.lean#L210-L219","doc":"The (2,1) Borromean character is the trace of an explicit triple\nproduct of 2×2 matrices in the standard rep — a finite expression\nin the t-parameter algebra (no `sorry` needed for the definition). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.stdRep3_chi_borromean","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.stdRep3_chi_borromean","kind":"def","line":202,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HeckeH3.lean#L202-L208","doc":"The (2,1) Wedderburn character of the Borromean braid β_Bor =\n(σ₀ σ₁⁻¹)^3 ∈ B₃.\n\nComputed by: forming the matrix M = σ₀ · σ₁⁻¹ in (2,1), cubing it,\nand taking the trace. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.stdRep3_M_cubed_eq_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.stdRep3_M_cubed_eq_one","kind":"theorem","line":141,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HeckeH3.lean#L141-L178","doc":"**Structural identity** (PR derivation 2026-05-24): in the standard\n(2,1) representation of H₃(q), the cube of σ₀σ₁ is the identity\nmatrix, exactly, for all q.\n\nDirect consequence: the matrix M = σ₀σ₁ has minimal polynomial\nX² + X + 1, whose roots are the primitive cube roots of unity\ne^{±2πi/3} = −1/2 ± i√3/2.  These eigenvalues are q-independent.\n\n**Corollary for T(3, n) torus knots.**  The braid word for the\nT(3, n) torus knot family is (σ₀σ₁)^n in B₃.  The (2,1) character\nis therefore\n    χ^{(2,1)}((σ₀σ₁)^n)  =  2 cos(2πn/3)  ∈  {−1, −1, +2}\ncyclically with n mod 3 — **q-independent**.\n\nThis means the Fibonacci/Chebyshev-of-second-kind h-polynomial\npattern proved for T(2, 2m) in H₂(q) (PR #1165) does NOT extend\nto T(3, n) via the (2,1) channel of H₃(q): the (2,1) contribution\nis a pure 3-cycle character with no h-dependence.\n\nThe non-trivial q-dependence of J_{T(3, n)}(q) lives entirely in\nthe trivial (q^{2n}) and sign (q^{-2n}) Wedderburn channels.\n\n**Computational provenance**: sympy-verified at q symbolic in\n[`computations/probes/t3n_binomial_pattern_probe.py`]. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.stdRep3_braid","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.stdRep3_braid","kind":"theorem","line":125,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HeckeH3.lean#L125-L137","doc":"The braid relation σ₀σ₁σ₀ = σ₁σ₀σ₁ in the standard representation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.stdRep3_hecke1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.stdRep3_hecke1","kind":"theorem","line":111,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HeckeH3.lean#L111-L121","doc":"σ₁ satisfies the Hecke relation in the standard representation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.stdRep3_hecke0","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.stdRep3_hecke0","kind":"theorem","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HeckeH3.lean#L99-L109","doc":"σ₀ satisfies the Hecke relation in the standard representation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.q_from_t_sub_HA_t","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.q_from_t_sub_HA_t","kind":"theorem","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HeckeH3.lean#L92-L95","doc":"`q − HA = q⁻¹` in `R_t` (pure ring identity, no `t·t⁻¹` relation). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.stdRep3_genInv1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.stdRep3_genInv1","kind":"def","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HeckeH3.lean#L72-L77","doc":"Generator inverse σ₁⁻¹ in the standard (2,1) representation.\n\n`σ₁⁻¹ = σ₁ − HA · I = ⎡ −q     0  ⎤`\n`⎣  1    q⁻¹ ⎦` ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.stdRep3_genInv0","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.stdRep3_genInv0","kind":"def","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HeckeH3.lean#L65-L70","doc":"Generator inverse σ₀⁻¹ in the standard (2,1) representation.\n\n`σ₀⁻¹ = σ₀ − HA · I = ⎡ q⁻¹   1  ⎤`\n`⎣ 0    −q  ⎦` ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.stdRep3_gen1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.stdRep3_gen1","kind":"def","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HeckeH3.lean#L54-L63","doc":"Generator σ₁ in the standard (2,1) representation of H₃(q).\n\n```\nσ₁ = ⎡ −q⁻¹   0 ⎤\n     ⎣  1      q ⎦\n```\n\nEigenvalues: q (bottom-right) and −q⁻¹ (top-left). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.stdRep3_gen0","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.stdRep3_gen0","kind":"def","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HeckeH3.lean#L43-L52","doc":"Generator σ₀ in the standard (2,1) representation of H₃(q).\n\n```\nσ₀ = ⎡ q   1  ⎤\n     ⎣ 0  −q⁻¹ ⎦\n```\n\nEigenvalues: q (top-left) and −q⁻¹ (bottom-right). ","signatureChunk":0}]}